Dependency scope and versions

Source incorporated into native artifacts (versions are locked in
hyper_multicore/_build/dependencies.lock.json):
- ops-nn v9.1.0.pre:
  selected RMSNorm/SwiGLU source primitives, with local patches.
  Source: https://gitcode.com/cann/ops-nn.git
- ops-transformer: GMM v9.1.0.pre and the MHC sources selected by the lock file:
  selected GMM/MHC source primitives, with local patches.
  Source: https://gitcode.com/cann/ops-transformer.git
- CANN SHMEM (source version selected by the lock file):
  private SDK/runtime libraries built with the component's locked patches.
  Source: https://gitcode.com/cann/shmem.git
  These three repositories use CANN Open Software License Agreement Version 2.0;
  their license texts are reproduced below.

Framework headers incorporated by compiling the Torch/SHMEM adapters:
- PyTorch and torch-npu headers come from the selected framework installation.
- pybind11 headers are supplied by Torch's include/pybind11 tree, not selected
  from a separately installed pybind11 package. The initial seven-framework
  matrix supplies header versions 2.13.6, 3.0.1, 3.0.4 and 3.1.0 through the
  corresponding Torch wheels; the primary BSD license is reproduced below.
  Actual framework build identities are recorded per adapter in build_info.json.

External runtime dependencies, not bundled as complete distributions:
- PyTorch and torch-npu shared libraries: the actual framework versions and ABI
  are recorded per adapter in build_info.json. Single-framework wheel metadata
  pins its actual Torch build; full-matrix wheels retain a general Torch
  dependency and select a branch-specific adapter at runtime.
- NumPy (numpy>=1.26,<2): Python runtime dependency, provided separately.
- CANN toolkit/ops, Ascend driver and system libraries: supplied by the runtime
  environment, separate from the locked CANN source repositories listed above.

The original PyTorch primary BSD notice is retained below. The torch-npu primary
